---
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import BrandMark from "../../components/BrandMark.astro";
import SiteSearch from "../../components/SiteSearch.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/blocks/Callout.astro";
import PullQuote from "../../components/blocks/PullQuote.astro";
import EvidenceLinkBlock from "../../components/blocks/EvidenceLinkBlock.astro";
import { houseIndexNavigation, primaryNavigation } from "../fixtures";
---

<div class="workshop-page">
  <SiteHeader
    currentPath="/dispatches/"
    links={primaryNavigation}
    houseIndexLinks={houseIndexNavigation}
  >
    <BrandMark slot="brand" />
    <SiteSearch pages={[]} />
  </SiteHeader>
  <main class="container article-shell">
    <article>
      <header class="article-header">
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">WOODHOUSE</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <a href="/dispatches/">STORIES</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <span>FIELD NOTE</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="article-title">Bubbles: a better second attempt.</h1>
        <p class="article-meta">Field note · Reviewed 23 October 2026</p>
        <p class="article-deck">
          One board, no shot limit. Fewest Shots gives the familiar bubble shooter a different
          reason to try again: improve the clear, rather than chase a bigger score.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="article-body">
        <div class="article-prose">
          <p class="article-lede">
            Bubbles gives the same aiming problem two different goals. In Classic, a large drop can
            be worth more than a quick clear. In Fewest Shots, clearing the board in fewer shots is
            the point.
          </p>
          <p>
            Bubbles is a browser bubble shooter. Aim, match three or more, and remove the bubbles
            holding the rest of the board up. The pleasure is in seeing an angle become an opening:
            a useful match can bring down more than the cluster you hit.
          </p>
          <PullQuote
            value={{
              quote: "A useful second attempt starts with a goal a player can understand."
            }}
          />
          <h2>Start with one decision.</h2>
          <p>
            Fewest Shots takes that familiar action and gives it a clear finish. There is one board
            and no shot limit. The question is not how long you can last, but how few shots the
            board needs.
          </p>
          <Callout
            value={{
              kind: "boundary",
              title: "What this does not prove",
              body: "A passing replay check is evidence for the replay, not for a person enjoying the game. Physical play and adoption need their own observations."
            }}
          />
          <EvidenceLinkBlock
            value={{
              evidence_key: "bubbles-replay-check",
              context:
                "The replay check is the evidence behind the competition claim. Read the record before treating a score as verified.",
              label: "Read the replay-check record"
            }}
          />
        </div>
        <aside class="article-rail" aria-label="Article evidence">
          <div class="rail-block">
            <span class="rail-label">Evidence reviewed</span>
            <strong>2026-10-23</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="rail-block">
            <span class="rail-label">What changed</span>
            <p>A useful personal challenge starts with a goal a player can understand.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rail-block">
            <span class="rail-label">Proof boundary</span>
            <p>This is an edited public record, not a private source transcript.</p>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter links={primaryNavigation} reviewDateLabel="6 November 2026" />
</div>

<style>
  .workshop-page {
    background: var(--ink);
  }
  .article-shell {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }
  .article-header {
    max-width: 68rem;
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .article-title {
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .article-meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 500 0.72rem/1.5 var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .article-deck {
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--copy);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.7vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .article-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(14rem, 0.36fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }
  .article-prose {
    max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .article-prose h2 {
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .article-lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .article-rail {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .rail-block {
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .rail-block strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  .rail-block p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--copy-soft);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }
  .rail-label {
    color: var(--brass);
    font: 600 0.6rem/1.4 var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .article-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .article-rail {
      order: -1;
    }
  }
</style>
